Dialogue: 3,0:09:19.44,0:09:25.19,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SHOTEX FLU VACCINATION EVENT
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.80,0:09:43.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In 1918, flu and pneumonia killed almost as many
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.35,0:09:45.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}American soldiers as combat did.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.71,0:09:49.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}There was no vaccine, and no antibiotics for the
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.26,0:09:51.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}pneumonia that followed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.03,0:09:54.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}27 years later, the first of those answers arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.80,0:09:58.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A licensed flu vaccine, built with the Army's help.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:40.05,0:09:45.80,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1146 0 l 1146 132 l 0 132{\p0}
